module

-- **Yours (H).** A front-end theorem: what the rule proofs stand on. It arrives
-- as a `sorry` and a signature install leaves it alone.
--
-- **Non-vacuity** — that a well-formed model exists at all.
--
-- Easy to overlook and fatal to omit. Soundness says the assumptions of a
-- checked proof hold in *no* well-formed model. If `model_wf` were satisfied by
-- nothing, that would be true of every proof, and the whole development would
-- prove nothing while appearing to prove everything.
--
-- Could arrive proven: it asks for one model, and the obvious one — every
-- symbol mapped to the default value of its type — is generated. In Logos the
-- corresponding file constructs exactly that.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- What Logos does here
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- `Cpc/Proofs/TypePreservation/Nonvacuity.lean`, and it is **104 lines** -- by
-- far the cheapest thing on this list.
--
-- The proof constructs a model rather than arguing one exists: every symbol is
-- mapped to a default value of its declared type, and the three conjuncts of
-- `model_wf` are then discharged against that construction. It reduces to one
-- lemma about the value types -- that every well-formed type has a canonical
-- inhabitant -- and the rest is bookkeeping.
--
-- So the shape to copy is: find a canonical inhabitant per type, then the model
-- is immediate. If your types are the stock SMT-LIB ones this is nearly free.
--
-- **Whether it can be inherited depends on your `smt.eos`.** The statement is
-- about definitions generated from the SMT-LIB semantics, so a proof of it
-- transfers only while that semantics is the stock one — which is exactly what
-- the `logos-smt` entry of `install/defs/profile.conf` records. Supply your own
-- `smt.eos`, change what a type is or what a well-formed model is, and this
-- becomes yours no matter what upstream ships.
public import @CALCULUS@.ModelWf
import all @CALCULUS@.ModelWf

@[expose] public section

namespace Smtm

/-- Well-formed models exist. -/
theorem model_wf_nonvacuous : ∃ M : SmtModel, model_wf M := by
  sorry

end Smtm
